## 4. Required source-of-truth design

Every stored chunk MUST have stable traceable provenance.

Never store anonymous text chunks.

Every chunk must contain metadata equivalent to:

```json
{
  "chunk_id": "stable UUID",
  "document_id": "stable UUID",
  "document_version": "string or hash",
  "content": "cleaned source content",
  "book": "book title if available",
  "author": "Pandit Shriram Sharma Acharya or verified author",
  "chapter": "chapter title if available",
  "section": "section title if available",
  "page_start": 1,
  "page_end": 1,
  "language": "hi | en | mixed",
  "source_type": "book | speech | discourse | article",
  "edition": "optional",
  "publication": "optional",
  "source_url": "optional verified URL",
  "copyright_status": "approved | pending | restricted",
  "quality_status": "pending | approved | rejected",
  "extraction_method": "pdf_text | ocr",
  "ocr_confidence": "optional numeric value",
  "content_hash": "hash",
  "parser_version": "version",
  "chunker_version": "version",
  "embedding_model": "model name"
}
```

The system must preserve:

- Raw original PDF
- Extracted page text
- OCR output where applicable
- Cleaned text
- Page numbers
- Metadata
- Chunk IDs
- Document version
- Ingestion logs
- Quality status

Never lose the connection between a chunk and its original source page(s).

