## 5. Ingestion rules

### Required ingestion flow

```text
Authorized PDF
    ↓
Create document record and ingestion run
    ↓
Extract text page by page
    ↓
Assess extraction quality
    ├── Good digital text → use it
    └── Missing/poor text → OCR fallback
    ↓
Store raw extracted/OCR text
    ↓
Normalize and clean text
    ↓
Detect language
    ↓
Detect title/chapter/section structure where possible
    ↓
Run quality checks
    ↓
Create page-aware, section-aware chunks
    ↓
Embed approved chunks
    ↓
Store chunks and embeddings
    ↓
Mark document ingestion status
```

### OCR requirements

Hindi OCR is a high-risk area.

Before indexing OCR output:

- Preserve OCR output page by page
- Flag low-confidence or suspicious pages
- Detect broken Unicode, garbage characters, missing matras, repeated text,
  malformed Devanagari, and excessive symbols
- Compare representative extracted pages with the original PDF visually
- Do not automatically mark low-quality OCR as approved
- Support manual document/page review when needed

Bad OCR must never silently enter the production index.

### Quality checks

Implement checks for:

- Empty pages
- Empty chunks
- Chunks that are too short to be meaningful
- Duplicate chunks
- Duplicate pages
- Excessive OCR garbage
- Broken Unicode
- Repeated headers and footers
- Page number contamination
- Missing document ID
- Missing page range
- Unsupported language
- Unapproved copyright/access status
- Missing or invalid metadata

Only chunks with `quality_status = approved` can be retrieved by default.

