## 10. Conversation memory rules

Conversation history may help interpret follow-up questions, but it is NOT
evidence.

Use history only to rewrite an ambiguous follow-up into a standalone retrieval
query.

Example:

```text
User: “गुरुदेव ने ब्रह्मचर्य के बारे में क्या कहा?”
User: “इसे daily life में कैसे follow करें?”

Rewritten retrieval query:
“गुरुदेव के अनुसार ब्रह्मचर्य के सिद्धांतों को दैनिक जीवन में कैसे अपनाया जा सकता है?”
```

Then retrieve fresh source material.

Never answer a follow-up solely from chat history if retrieval does not find
supporting source material.

For production:

- Store conversation data persistently
- Link messages to conversation IDs and users where appropriate
- Define retention and deletion behavior
- Do not represent chat history as permanent user identity or spiritual profile
- Avoid storing sensitive personal information unless required and consented to

