## 12. Evaluation is mandatory

Do not evaluate quality by manually asking a few questions.

Create and maintain an evaluation dataset, for example:

```text
evals/
  golden_questions.json
  retrieval_results.json
  answer_results.json
```

Each test question should include:

```json
{
  "id": "q001",
  "question": "क्रोध को नियंत्रित करने के बारे में क्या उपाय बताए गए हैं?",
  "language": "hi",
  "answerable": true,
  "expected_document_id": "uuid",
  "expected_pages":,[42][43]
  "expected_topic": "क्रोध और आत्मसंयम"
}
```

Include:

- Hindi questions
- English questions
- Hinglish questions
- Exact keyword questions
- Conceptual questions
- Ambiguous questions
- Follow-up questions
- Questions requiring abstention
- Questions that have only partial support
- Questions across different books and source types

Measure at minimum:

- Hit@1
- Hit@3
- Hit@5
- MRR
- Context relevance
- Context recall
- Citation correctness
- Answer faithfulness
- Abstention correctness
- OCR quality acceptance rate
- Latency
- Cost per query

Never claim an advanced feature improves the product without comparing it
against a saved baseline evaluation result.

Run relevant tests and evaluations after changes to parsing, cleaning,
chunking, embeddings, retrieval, prompts, reranking, or answer generation.

